    "result": "Refresh trigger: server/index.ts, server/agent-runner.ts, and server/context-summarizer.ts changed to publish application-owned spend activity after OpenCode runs, while server/index.ts also gained an advisory intent-classifier consult ahead of the pure pre-flight gate and cost/duration fields on recorded pre-flight dispositions. A follow-up now bounds classifier context to the selected trigger and cancels routing when room activity changes during the consult. At upstream v1.18.25 (cb7d8b2f5e44876ef98b661dc10590c915af3a9f), re-inspected every recorded path for structured-sdk-server, cli-jsonl, model-discovery, permissions-and-tools, mcp-adapter, and native-setup-auth, and compared the affected upstream paths with v1.18.18 (31406ccc51b4bd2a4e1e086b2bcaa5f7f804f26d). Confirmed: CLI JSON event generation, session/provider telemetry, loopback server/SDK contracts, model listing, credential control routes, inline permission, and custom-tool discovery remain consumed through the existing invocation and parser boundaries. The application-owned callbacks and classifier consult do not change OpenCode arguments, transport selection, permissions, tool schemas, provider transforms, credentials, or upstream session semantics. The recorded focused contract tests pass.",
